# scripts/.schema-drift-allowlist
#
# Tables that ARE referenced by code AND do exist on the production database
# but are NOT declared by any file under supabase/migrations/. They were
# created out-of-band (manual psql, deleted/older migration runs, etc.).
#
# Goal: shrink this list to empty.
#
# Each entry should ideally have a follow-up PR that writes a back-fill
# migration mirroring the column definitions of the live table on prod
# (use `pg_dump --schema-only -t <table>` on the VPS to get the truth).
#
# Audited 2026-05-22 against the Contabo VPS (`SELECT tablename FROM
# pg_tables WHERE schemaname='public'`).
#
# Tables in code with NO declaring migration AND NOT present in prod DB
# are deliberately NOT in this list — those are real drift and the
# schema-drift CI check must fail until a migration is added.

# --- Telegram bot subsystem (live on prod, missing from migrations dir) ---
telegram_afk
telegram_antiraid_joins
telegram_antiraid_sessions
telegram_blacklist_settings
telegram_federation_admins
telegram_federation_bans
telegram_federation_members
telegram_federations
telegram_ticket_messages
telegram_tickets

# --- Userbot subsystem (live on prod, missing from migrations dir) ---
userbot_filters
userbot_gbans
userbot_notes
userbot_pm_permit

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REAL DRIFT — needs a backfill migration. These tables ARE referenced by
# code but are NOT in the prod DB *and* not declared in supabase/migrations/.
# Calls to these tables silently no-op in production (Supabase client
# returns { data: null, error: 'relation does not exist' } and most
# call-sites don't check `error`). Tracked for follow-up PRs.
#
# Each entry should be removed from this list when its declaring
# migration lands. Goal: this section empty.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Telegram feature tables (PR follow-up batch 1) ---
# Migrated by 061_telegram_feature_tables.sql — entries removed from list.

# --- Telegram code-vs-DB rename drift (PR follow-up batch 2) ---
# Resolved in PR #530 / migration 062: code now points at
# telegram_bot_configs.admin_only_mode and telegram_moderation_log.

# --- WhatsApp + misc tables (PR follow-up batch 3) ---
# Resolved in PR #531 / migration 063: schedule_templates, email_bounces,
# and bank_cashout_requests now have declaring migrations. `uploads` was
# a false positive (Supabase Storage bucket, not a table); the schema-drift
# regex now skips `.storage.from(...)` calls.
#
# Goal achieved: zero real drift remaining. The allowlist now contains
# only out-of-band-created tables that exist on prod but are not in
# supabase/migrations/. Folding those into migrations is a separate
# cleanup task (lower priority — they work, they're just not declared).
